Also, when you’re ready to hand over a proposed setup, just use a tiny JSON snippet like this so it’s easy to parse:

{
  "solution": {
    "selected": [<clinic_to_open>, <clinic_to_open>, ...],
    "assignments": [<neighborhood_chosen_clinic>, <neighborhood_chosen_clinic>, ...]
  }
}

Pretty simple: "selected" is the list of clinic sites you plan to open, and "assignments" lists, in the same order as the neighborhoods in the instance, which open clinic each neighborhood will use. Think of it like filling out a form — which clinics are on, and for each neighborhood which clinic they go to.

This JSON is just the expected shape (a sketch), not the final answer.

