Out in the field, the food bank team must choose a handful of distribution points to staff and then direct every recipient area to exactly one of those staffed points. Each staffed point has a price tag to keep it open and each assignment from a point to an area has a delivery cost, so the best-looking plan is the one with the lowest total cost — add the staffing cost of each open point to all the delivery costs for the assignments. Each area must be covered once and only once, and each staffed point has a maximum amount it can serve, so assignments must stay within those limits. The concrete figures are provided below.

